1
00:00:34,013 --> 00:00:35,348
Are you in position?

2
00:00:36,141 --> 00:00:37,851
<i>All set.</i>

3
00:00:43,439 --> 00:00:44,941
Thank you.

4
00:00:50,905 --> 00:00:54,284
Hey. The trunk.
What are you doing, slowpoke?

5
00:00:55,285 --> 00:00:56,619
He’s here.

6
00:00:56,703 --> 00:01:00,081
That’s Ishikawa,
the president of River Productions.

7
00:01:02,208 --> 00:01:04,961
He’s got that same sleazy face as always.

8
00:01:05,044 --> 00:01:06,921
Alright, Habu, I’m counting on you.

9
00:01:07,005 --> 00:01:08,965
-Here is your room key.
-Thanks.

10
00:01:09,048 --> 00:01:10,466
Enjoy your stay.

11
00:01:12,051 --> 00:01:14,470
-What are you doing? Leave already.
-I'm sorry.

12
00:01:14,554 --> 00:01:16,514
Sir, I will guide you to your room.

13
00:01:16,598 --> 00:01:18,683
No, thank you. It's all right.

14
00:01:18,766 --> 00:01:20,602
-I'll carry your luggage.
-I'm fine.

15
00:01:21,311 --> 00:01:23,563
-Please, allow me--
-I told you…

16
00:01:24,355 --> 00:01:25,773
I don't need help.

17
00:01:26,316 --> 00:01:27,317
My apologies.

18
00:01:27,400 --> 00:01:28,735
Seriously!

19
00:01:31,070 --> 00:01:32,280
Leave it to me.

20
00:01:35,867 --> 00:01:38,161
Oh, excuse me.

21
00:01:38,244 --> 00:01:40,246
-Which floor?
-18th floor, please.

22
00:01:41,581 --> 00:01:43,291
Thank you.

23
00:01:49,631 --> 00:01:51,674
-The 19th floor.
-<i>Understood.</i>

24
00:01:51,758 --> 00:01:54,219
<i>The 19th floor, right? Heading there now.</i>

25
00:02:02,518 --> 00:02:04,020
Room 1926.

26
00:02:28,002 --> 00:02:30,463
His room key is in
the left back pocket of his pants.

27
00:02:37,470 --> 00:02:39,430
-Ow! Hey!
-Ouch!

28
00:02:39,514 --> 00:02:42,058
Oh no, my racing tickets!

29
00:02:42,141 --> 00:02:43,935
Watch it, idiot.

30
00:02:44,811 --> 00:02:46,562
Huh? My winning ticket is gone.

31
00:02:46,646 --> 00:02:50,274
-Hey! Did you take it?
-I didn't. What the heck?

32
00:02:50,984 --> 00:02:53,027
-That's my phone.
-Your back pockets.

33
00:02:53,111 --> 00:02:54,529
Hey, that's creepy, man.

34
00:02:55,113 --> 00:02:57,615
-Huh?
-Don't take my wallet!

35
00:02:57,699 --> 00:03:00,243
-I don't know about your ticket!
-Oh, sorry!

36
00:03:00,326 --> 00:03:01,536
I found it.

37
00:03:02,370 --> 00:03:03,705
Sorry.

38
00:03:19,846 --> 00:03:21,431
Is this really okay?

39
00:03:21,514 --> 00:03:23,641
It's fine.

40
00:03:25,893 --> 00:03:27,770
It's locked!

41
00:03:28,312 --> 00:03:29,814
Four, one, zero.

42
00:03:29,897 --> 00:03:31,482
Two, two, three.

43
00:03:31,566 --> 00:03:33,359
That's the code he usually uses.

44
00:03:33,443 --> 00:03:35,987
<i>Four, one, zero.</i>

45
00:03:36,070 --> 00:03:38,614
Two, two, three.

46
00:03:39,365 --> 00:03:40,325
It's open.

47
00:03:40,408 --> 00:03:41,492
Now…

48
00:03:47,540 --> 00:03:48,374
HIKARI TAKENAKA

49
00:03:48,458 --> 00:03:50,460
Nakazaki, where is the fingerprint film?

50
00:03:52,503 --> 00:03:55,757
I've seen this in anime,
but it actually works?

51
00:04:02,013 --> 00:04:03,556
Do you always do this sort of thing?

52
00:04:03,639 --> 00:04:05,641
It's a life hack.

53
00:04:08,519 --> 00:04:10,271
TRANSFERRING DATA

54
00:04:10,355 --> 00:04:12,774
<i>I'm so glad Hikari</i>
<i>got to star in that commercial.</i>

55
00:04:12,857 --> 00:04:14,734
Thank you as always.

56
00:04:14,817 --> 00:04:16,944
It's all thanks to you, Mr. Tajima.

57
00:04:17,737 --> 00:04:19,530
I'm sure Nishiguchi is happy too.

58
00:04:19,614 --> 00:04:21,657
He's her manager, after all.

59
00:04:21,741 --> 00:04:24,452
He's useless,
so I was thinking of replacing him soon.

60
00:04:25,078 --> 00:04:26,537
Excuse me.

61
00:04:26,621 --> 00:04:28,456
I brought your drinks.

62
00:04:28,539 --> 00:04:30,041
Just set them down here.

63
00:04:30,124 --> 00:04:31,751
Oh, understood, sir.

64
00:04:31,834 --> 00:04:33,836
-My son's calling.
-Go ahead.

65
00:04:35,129 --> 00:04:37,590
Hey, give me a break, you bastard!

66
00:04:37,673 --> 00:04:38,925
-I'm so sorry!
-Get me a towel.

67
00:04:39,008 --> 00:04:40,676
-A towel?
-You have one right there!

68
00:04:40,760 --> 00:04:42,261
I do, sorry.

69
00:04:42,345 --> 00:04:45,223
-What are you doing?
-I'm so sorry.

70
00:04:45,306 --> 00:04:47,100
-That's too many towels!
-Sorry.

71
00:04:47,183 --> 00:04:48,309
How is Yuuki doing?

72
00:04:48,393 --> 00:04:50,645
Sorry. Today is canceled.
Let's reschedule.

73
00:04:50,728 --> 00:04:52,105
Why so suddenly?

74
00:04:52,188 --> 00:04:53,231
Mr. Tajima!

75
00:04:56,109 --> 00:04:57,443
I'm sorry.

76
00:04:58,736 --> 00:05:00,363
-So sorry.
-That's enough.

77
00:05:00,446 --> 00:05:02,281
Excuse me. I'm sorry!

78
00:05:05,785 --> 00:05:06,994
Hello?

79
00:05:07,078 --> 00:05:09,038
Sorry. I'll get changed and head over.

80
00:05:09,122 --> 00:05:10,373
Okay.

81
00:05:16,295 --> 00:05:18,005
I'm sorry. My apologies.

82
00:05:18,089 --> 00:05:20,425
<i>S-Sabayama here! I'm sorry.</i>

83
00:05:20,508 --> 00:05:22,427
<i>Ishikawa went back to his room!</i>

84
00:05:22,510 --> 00:05:24,053
<i>Why so soon?</i>

85
00:05:24,137 --> 00:05:27,014
<i>-How much time is left?</i>
<i>-Three minutes remaining.</i>

86
00:05:29,350 --> 00:05:30,726
I'll leave the rest to you.

87
00:05:30,810 --> 00:05:32,895
-Hey, hold on!
-Where are you going?

88
00:05:33,855 --> 00:05:35,815
<i>Mr. Uramawashi, what should we do?</i>

89
00:05:35,898 --> 00:05:37,066
<i>Are you listening?</i>

90
00:05:37,150 --> 00:05:39,068
<i>We're still copying the files.</i>

91
00:05:39,569 --> 00:05:41,779
MINUTES LEFT

92
00:05:45,283 --> 00:05:46,409
Huh?

93
00:05:46,492 --> 00:05:48,077
There you are!

94
00:05:48,161 --> 00:05:51,164
I accidentally picked up your key earlier.

95
00:05:52,123 --> 00:05:52,999
I'm sorry.

96
00:05:53,082 --> 00:05:54,167
What?

97
00:05:54,250 --> 00:05:55,960
Why give him the key?

98
00:05:56,043 --> 00:05:57,587
<i>Seriously…</i>

99
00:06:03,301 --> 00:06:05,136
I am very sorry.

100
00:06:07,096 --> 00:06:08,639
You too, sir?

101
00:06:08,723 --> 00:06:11,267
There is currently an issue
with the room keys.

102
00:06:11,350 --> 00:06:13,144
Please replace it at the front desk.

103
00:06:13,227 --> 00:06:14,437
Are you serious?

104
00:06:14,520 --> 00:06:16,564
We apologize for the inconvenience.

105
00:06:24,864 --> 00:06:26,574
We are very sorry.

106
00:06:27,950 --> 00:06:30,703
Of course it's a fake.

107
00:06:31,329 --> 00:06:32,496
ONE MINUTE LEFT

108
00:06:32,580 --> 00:06:33,873
DATA TRANSFER COMPLETE

109
00:06:35,750 --> 00:06:39,086
<i>-You should have told us.</i>
<i>-Sorry.</i>

110
00:06:40,421 --> 00:06:42,048
Good work, everyone.

111
00:06:47,220 --> 00:06:49,889
<i>The damages trial between</i>
<i>Mr. Shuto Ishikawa,</i>

112
00:06:49,972 --> 00:06:51,849
<i>president of an entertainment agency,</i>

113
00:06:51,933 --> 00:06:55,895
<i>and the defendant, a former manager,</i>
<i>is about to begin.</i>

114
00:06:56,687 --> 00:06:58,022
Mr. Ishikawa,

115
00:06:58,940 --> 00:07:03,027
you claim that because Hikari Takenaka,
a talent under your agency,

116
00:07:03,110 --> 00:07:05,821
dropped out of a commercial
due to Mr. Nishiguchi harassing her,

117
00:07:05,905 --> 00:07:11,452
your agency had to pay
100 million yen in penalties. Correct?

118
00:07:12,203 --> 00:07:13,329
That's right.

119
00:07:13,871 --> 00:07:17,583
Because of him, our entire agency
is being slandered online.

120
00:07:17,667 --> 00:07:19,585
That's strange.

121
00:07:19,669 --> 00:07:21,963
It differs from Mr. Nishiguchi's claim.

122
00:07:22,797 --> 00:07:25,716
That means one of you is lying.

123
00:07:25,800 --> 00:07:27,927
I'm the victim here!

124
00:07:28,010 --> 00:07:30,763
-Obviously, Nishiguchi is the one lying!
-No!

125
00:07:33,432 --> 00:07:34,559
Your Honor.

126
00:07:35,142 --> 00:07:37,895
I would like to submit
additional evidence.

127
00:07:38,479 --> 00:07:40,606
COMPANY APP "RVPRO"
HAS BEEN FOUND TO BE SPYWARE

128
00:07:40,690 --> 00:07:42,942
HIKARI TAKENAKA

129
00:07:43,025 --> 00:07:44,777
WHY DO YOU HAVE THOSE PHOTOS? DELETE THEM

130
00:07:44,860 --> 00:07:45,945
WE CAN LEAK THEM, THEN?

131
00:07:46,028 --> 00:07:47,780
Why do you have this data?

132
00:07:47,863 --> 00:07:51,409
You were blackmailing Hikari
and other actors,

133
00:07:51,492 --> 00:07:54,829
forcing them into work against their will.

134
00:07:54,912 --> 00:07:58,207
Your Honor, this has no relevance
to the case at hand.

135
00:07:58,291 --> 00:08:00,251
Defense counsel, please continue.

136
00:08:00,876 --> 00:08:06,173
For those who didn't comply,
you used this data to threaten them.

137
00:08:06,799 --> 00:08:08,217
WE CAN LEAK THEM, THEN?

138
00:08:08,301 --> 00:08:09,635
TO QUIT, PAY THE FIVE MILLION YEN

139
00:08:09,719 --> 00:08:11,554
PLEASE DON'T RELEASE THAT VIDEO

140
00:08:11,637 --> 00:08:13,264
No! This isn't true!

141
00:08:14,307 --> 00:08:19,437
They say that to maintain one lie,
you need twenty more.

142
00:08:24,191 --> 00:08:28,195
Scumbags who think nothing
of sacrificing others…

143
00:08:29,071 --> 00:08:30,948
shouldn't try to lie.

144
00:08:32,033 --> 00:08:32,867
Scumbags?

145
00:08:35,786 --> 00:08:40,124
Only a perfected lie
can overcome the truth.

146
00:08:43,628 --> 00:08:45,212
That is all from me.

147
00:09:04,482 --> 00:09:08,486
If you keep at this, you'll lose
your license to practice someday.

148
00:09:09,111 --> 00:09:11,864
Mr. Uramawashi, do you have a moment?

149
00:09:11,947 --> 00:09:14,450
Do you plan to pursue
the Ishikawa case further?

150
00:09:14,533 --> 00:09:17,536
There are accusations that
you obtained the evidence illegally!

151
00:09:17,620 --> 00:09:18,663
Please answer us!

152
00:09:21,916 --> 00:09:27,254
The truth was painted over with lies.
All I did was use lies to reclaim it.

153
00:09:42,895 --> 00:09:44,939
Habu! Carry this!

154
00:09:45,022 --> 00:09:46,941
But you lost at rock-paper-scissors.

155
00:09:47,942 --> 00:09:50,277
Because of that plan, my work's piling up.

156
00:09:50,361 --> 00:09:52,697
Don't spill water
on the target again, okay?

157
00:09:52,780 --> 00:09:57,743
-It succeeded, so what's the problem?
-Well, that's because I had your back.

158
00:09:58,703 --> 00:09:59,954
Bastard.

159
00:10:00,663 --> 00:10:03,290
Hey, how many times do I have to tell you!

160
00:10:03,374 --> 00:10:05,292
It's always the same thing!

161
00:10:05,376 --> 00:10:06,919
CUBE HOTEL INFILTRATION PLAN

162
00:10:07,002 --> 00:10:09,380
Nakazaki, congrats on your debut.

163
00:10:09,463 --> 00:10:11,298
You have a knack for this.

164
00:10:11,382 --> 00:10:14,385
I only wanted a normal
part-time job at a law firm.

165
00:10:14,468 --> 00:10:19,181
Boss, once again,
we are deeply in the red.

166
00:10:19,807 --> 00:10:23,602
Well, all necessary expenses,
to bring smiles to people's faces!

167
00:10:26,564 --> 00:10:28,941
Victory drinks sure taste good.

168
00:10:30,818 --> 00:10:33,904
Drinking is fine,
but please do your work properly.

169
00:10:33,988 --> 00:10:34,989
This!

170
00:10:35,614 --> 00:10:38,242
We haven't even finished
the initial blueprints!

171
00:10:40,536 --> 00:10:42,246
I'm talking to you too, Habu!

172
00:10:42,788 --> 00:10:44,457
-It's time to head home.
-What?

173
00:10:44,540 --> 00:10:45,416
-See you.
-Bye.

174
00:10:45,499 --> 00:10:47,918
Wait, we're still working, so help us out.

175
00:10:48,002 --> 00:10:49,545
We don't pay overtime.

176
00:10:50,629 --> 00:10:52,298
Wait, I don't get paid either?

177
00:10:52,381 --> 00:10:54,884
Sorry, my hours are discretionary.

178
00:10:54,967 --> 00:10:56,385
Well then, bye.

179
00:10:56,469 --> 00:10:58,345
-Wait!
-See you.

180
00:10:59,930 --> 00:11:01,682
Mr. Uramawashi!

181
00:11:01,766 --> 00:11:03,434
Is the plan revision ready yet?

182
00:11:03,517 --> 00:11:05,019
Being a lawyer is fine,

183
00:11:05,102 --> 00:11:07,480
but please focus
on the architecture side too.

184
00:11:09,315 --> 00:11:11,776
This is it.

185
00:11:12,526 --> 00:11:14,904
No, this one…

186
00:11:14,987 --> 00:11:18,866
-Hey.
-Guggenheim, as designed by Gehry.

187
00:11:21,660 --> 00:11:25,456
These curves are so pretty,
no matter how many times I look at them.

188
00:11:25,539 --> 00:11:26,707
I knew it,

189
00:11:27,541 --> 00:11:31,462
we gotta go with an organic form.

190
00:11:31,545 --> 00:11:33,088
No!

191
00:11:33,172 --> 00:11:35,049
Whether as a lawyer or an architect,

192
00:11:35,132 --> 00:11:38,344
shouldn't client preferences
come before your own tastes?

193
00:11:38,427 --> 00:11:40,513
Hey, work before drinking.

194
00:11:40,596 --> 00:11:45,142
Rushing won't produce
anything good, right?

195
00:11:47,269 --> 00:11:49,647
No, not until I finish work! Habu!

196
00:11:49,730 --> 00:11:51,482
-Bring that over.
-Huh?

197
00:11:51,565 --> 00:11:54,944
-Can I just eat first…
-Hurry up!

198
00:11:55,861 --> 00:11:59,615
In the end, we couldn't get
Representative Tajima.

199
00:11:59,698 --> 00:12:01,825
He left so suddenly.

200
00:12:01,909 --> 00:12:04,703
He's got the devil's luck.

201
00:12:18,217 --> 00:12:19,969
By the way, he won again.

202
00:12:20,052 --> 00:12:23,264
-Won what?
-Shuto Ishikawa's trial.

203
00:12:23,347 --> 00:12:25,808
Mr. Uramawashi won brilliantly.

204
00:12:25,891 --> 00:12:28,143
I don't accept him as a lawyer.

205
00:12:28,227 --> 00:12:31,146
His hair is long,
and he doesn't dress properly in court.

206
00:12:31,230 --> 00:12:34,066
Well, that part is problematic.

207
00:12:34,149 --> 00:12:38,320
But he's protecting his clients,
so as a lawyer, isn't he a good one?

208
00:12:38,904 --> 00:12:41,699
Even so, his methods are not just.

209
00:12:41,782 --> 00:12:45,619
Yukari, you are too serious.
As a lawyer, that's a weakness.

210
00:12:47,246 --> 00:12:49,540
Oh, look at the time.

211
00:12:50,374 --> 00:12:53,210
-I'm off.
-Yukari, wait!

212
00:12:53,294 --> 00:12:54,753
-Good luck.
-Yes!

213
00:12:54,837 --> 00:12:57,256
<i>President of River Productions…</i>

214
00:12:57,339 --> 00:13:00,634
He made a mess of things.

215
00:13:01,719 --> 00:13:03,721
Now is an important period for me.

216
00:13:03,804 --> 00:13:06,181
I don't want any unnecessary trouble.

217
00:13:06,265 --> 00:13:08,475
All the cleanup
has already been completed.

218
00:13:08,559 --> 00:13:11,937
Oh. I'm glad you're a competent secretary.

219
00:13:12,730 --> 00:13:17,067
<i>-Our next story is…</i>
-Unlike some incompetent lawyer I know!

220
00:13:17,151 --> 00:13:21,447
<i>-The murder of Ms. Chiharu Aoi, 24…</i>
-Why was he even recommended?

221
00:13:21,530 --> 00:13:26,785
<i>Padam Garty, an Ulgovian, living in Ota,</i>
<i>has been indicted for murder.</i>

222
00:13:27,578 --> 00:13:31,290
<i>So far, he has denied all accusations.</i>

223
00:13:31,373 --> 00:13:33,542
SUSPECT CLAIMS
"I DIDN'T DO IT, I KNOW NOTHING"

224
00:13:35,753 --> 00:13:37,921
Nice to meet you, Mr. Padam.

225
00:13:38,631 --> 00:13:41,467
I am attorney Yukari Aso.

226
00:13:41,550 --> 00:13:43,510
I will be your defense attorney.

227
00:13:44,136 --> 00:13:45,262
I didn't kill anyone.

228
00:13:47,264 --> 00:13:51,518
But the apartment CCTV
captured you, right?

229
00:13:52,269 --> 00:13:55,314
I only went there to deliver a package.

230
00:13:55,397 --> 00:13:57,566
No one believes me, not even the police.

231
00:13:59,193 --> 00:14:01,111
I believe you.

232
00:14:01,737 --> 00:14:05,324
So please, believe in me too.

233
00:14:06,909 --> 00:14:08,744
-Hello.
-Hello.

234
00:14:09,620 --> 00:14:10,746
Ms. Aso!

235
00:14:11,372 --> 00:14:14,333
Mr. Moriki wants you to go to his office.

236
00:14:15,751 --> 00:14:19,380
-Falsely accused?
-Yes, he denies committing the crime.

237
00:14:19,463 --> 00:14:23,384
For the prosecutors to decide to indict,
they must have a lot of evidence.

238
00:14:23,467 --> 00:14:27,346
But this case feels rushed
and based on circumstantial evidence.

239
00:14:27,429 --> 00:14:30,015
You always charge ahead
with your sense of justice,

240
00:14:30,099 --> 00:14:31,976
but can you stop that already?

241
00:14:32,059 --> 00:14:33,769
Before long, you will…

242
00:14:35,187 --> 00:14:36,313
Ouch.

243
00:14:37,022 --> 00:14:40,442
Thanks to you, Ms. Aso,
I have to keep stomach medicine on me.

244
00:14:40,526 --> 00:14:43,237
Please take care of yourself. Excuse me.

245
00:14:49,118 --> 00:14:50,285
Hello.

246
00:14:50,369 --> 00:14:51,787
Hello!

247
00:14:54,540 --> 00:14:57,668
MR. PADAM GARTY
MURDER CASE

248
00:14:59,253 --> 00:15:00,629
This case…

249
00:15:00,713 --> 00:15:03,007
You have a 0.1% chance of winning.

250
00:15:03,090 --> 00:15:05,884
We can win one in a thousand times.

251
00:15:05,968 --> 00:15:09,430
Protecting the client
is the only correct answer for a lawyer.

252
00:15:09,513 --> 00:15:12,808
No chance of you giving up I see.

253
00:15:16,979 --> 00:15:19,440
JUSTICE'S FORM

254
00:15:21,942 --> 00:15:23,110
Here.

255
00:15:24,194 --> 00:15:26,030
I want a bit more openness.

256
00:15:26,113 --> 00:15:28,574
I will look into removing the partition.

257
00:15:28,657 --> 00:15:30,659
Also, I want to add more pillars.

258
00:15:30,743 --> 00:15:31,869
Pillars?

259
00:15:32,536 --> 00:15:34,705
Okay. What are the hiring conditions?

260
00:15:34,788 --> 00:15:39,084
Smart, able to read the room,
and good at lying.

261
00:15:39,168 --> 00:15:41,211
Understood. I will contact them.

262
00:15:42,421 --> 00:15:44,048
-Sabayama.
-Yes?

263
00:15:45,466 --> 00:15:48,594
Could you show me
that security camera footage?

264
00:15:48,677 --> 00:15:52,973
The police took the footage.

265
00:15:55,684 --> 00:15:57,519
But there's a backup, right?

266
00:15:57,603 --> 00:15:59,271
That was taken as well.

267
00:15:59,354 --> 00:16:01,607
"To preserve evidence," they said.

268
00:16:02,524 --> 00:16:04,109
I see.

269
00:16:05,110 --> 00:16:07,696
Then, please show me the crime scene.

270
00:16:18,290 --> 00:16:21,126
There's a breaker there?

271
00:16:21,210 --> 00:16:23,879
The resident liked to keep it hidden.

272
00:16:26,256 --> 00:16:29,218
How was the body when found?

273
00:16:29,301 --> 00:16:30,886
She didn't show up for work,

274
00:16:30,969 --> 00:16:33,764
so people from the club got worried
and came to check.

275
00:16:33,847 --> 00:16:36,642
She worked as a hostess, right?

276
00:16:37,392 --> 00:16:38,393
Yes.

277
00:16:38,477 --> 00:16:42,106
She was found collapsed,
bleeding from her head.

278
00:16:42,940 --> 00:16:44,358
Right over there.

279
00:16:53,617 --> 00:16:56,745
What was Ms. Chiharu like at the club?

280
00:16:57,996 --> 00:17:02,709
Chiharu was flirty, so customers often got
the wrong idea and hit on her.

281
00:17:03,252 --> 00:17:05,879
But she actually had a boyfriend.

282
00:17:05,963 --> 00:17:07,422
She was in a relationship?

283
00:17:07,506 --> 00:17:11,343
Yes. She was always bragging
that she was dating a bigshot's son.

284
00:17:12,094 --> 00:17:13,846
And on social media,

285
00:17:14,680 --> 00:17:16,974
she was often hinting at it.

286
00:17:18,559 --> 00:17:19,560
Huh?

287
00:17:20,686 --> 00:17:23,021
I'm pretty sure there was a photo of him…

288
00:17:23,105 --> 00:17:25,274
What kind of person was her boyfriend?

289
00:17:25,357 --> 00:17:29,319
He is the son of a Diet member,
Tajima something?

290
00:17:29,403 --> 00:17:32,447
-You shouldn't tell her that.
-He was a politician's son?

291
00:17:32,531 --> 00:17:37,911
Yes. At first she kept it a secret,
but she wanted to brag so badly.

292
00:17:37,995 --> 00:17:39,705
It was totally obvious.

293
00:17:39,788 --> 00:17:42,374
-Saki, you have a customer.
-Oh, okay!

294
00:17:42,457 --> 00:17:44,376
Sorry, I was asked for.

295
00:17:44,459 --> 00:17:46,295
Wait a moment.

296
00:17:48,547 --> 00:17:51,842
-Um…
-I wasn't close with Chiharu at all.

297
00:17:52,676 --> 00:17:55,596
-This is Saki!
-Hi, Saki!

298
00:17:55,679 --> 00:17:56,722
Thank you!

299
00:17:56,805 --> 00:17:58,724
Have a seat here.

300
00:18:04,813 --> 00:18:07,858
-I'LL VISIT AGAIN WHEN THINGS CALM DOWN
-REALLY? IT'S A PROMISE!

301
00:18:07,941 --> 00:18:11,153
A LAWYER CAME TO THE CLUB
SHE WAS ASKING ABOUT CHIHARU

302
00:18:13,947 --> 00:18:15,407
Shiori, you ask him too.

303
00:18:15,490 --> 00:18:19,369
-No.
-I need to give it some thought.

304
00:18:20,287 --> 00:18:23,165
The victim was apparently
in a relationship with Yuuki Tajima,

305
00:18:23,248 --> 00:18:25,876
Representative Tajima's son.
They planned for marriage.

306
00:18:25,959 --> 00:18:29,796
-You suspect him based on that?
-I am only discussing the possibility.

307
00:18:29,880 --> 00:18:34,134
-Don't look too much into this case.
-Why?!

308
00:18:34,218 --> 00:18:36,845
Consider who the players are.

309
00:18:36,929 --> 00:18:41,141
If you act recklessly,
it's not just you on the line.

310
00:18:41,225 --> 00:18:44,519
So you're saying we should just discard
people who are vulnerable?

311
00:18:44,603 --> 00:18:47,898
You want me to overlook
powerful people preying on the weak?

312
00:18:47,981 --> 00:18:51,276
What is questioned in court
is not righteousness,

313
00:18:51,360 --> 00:18:53,820
but facts built up from evidence.

314
00:18:54,363 --> 00:18:58,116
If you misunderstand that,
you cannot save your client.

315
00:19:03,956 --> 00:19:09,544
On the night of the incident, Yuuki Tajima
was having dinner with his father,

316
00:19:09,628 --> 00:19:11,421
Representative Tajima.

317
00:19:13,674 --> 00:19:15,926
HAVING DINNER WITH DAD TO CATCH UP
FAMILY TIME IS NICE ONCE IN A WHILE (LOL)

318
00:19:27,062 --> 00:19:28,939
Dad, I'm sorry.

319
00:19:29,022 --> 00:19:31,650
I had no idea a paparazzi was after me.

320
00:19:33,527 --> 00:19:35,737
Please sue this weekly magazine.

321
00:19:35,821 --> 00:19:39,199
Someone told me a weirdo came
to that club, asking questions.

322
00:19:39,283 --> 00:19:40,867
Very well.

323
00:19:40,951 --> 00:19:43,036
I'll prepare the lawsuit.

324
00:19:43,120 --> 00:19:44,913
You two, don't do anything!

325
00:19:46,039 --> 00:19:48,041
I'll ask this guy to handle it.

326
00:19:50,335 --> 00:19:51,878
Uramawashi?

327
00:19:52,754 --> 00:19:54,756
But at the recent trial, he was the one--

328
00:19:54,840 --> 00:19:57,843
I'm willing to make allies out of enemies.
That's my creed.

329
00:19:58,468 --> 00:20:02,848
Compared to those losers,
he is much more promising.

330
00:20:04,641 --> 00:20:09,563
If we throw enough money at him,
Uramawashi will work for us.

331
00:20:10,147 --> 00:20:11,565
A 30 percent markup, then.

332
00:20:11,648 --> 00:20:13,442
30 percent, huh?

333
00:20:13,525 --> 00:20:15,569
If we include all your requests,

334
00:20:15,652 --> 00:20:18,322
it seems it will
slightly exceed your budget.

335
00:20:18,405 --> 00:20:20,657
It might be a bit over budget.

336
00:20:20,741 --> 00:20:22,951
We can adjust based
on what you prioritize,

337
00:20:23,035 --> 00:20:24,911
so let's discuss it together.

338
00:20:24,995 --> 00:20:27,998
My fee is triple the market rate.
Is that acceptable?

339
00:20:28,999 --> 00:20:30,959
Huh? Triple?

340
00:20:31,043 --> 00:20:32,294
His fees are extortion.

341
00:20:32,377 --> 00:20:34,129
I recommend you stay away from him.

342
00:20:34,713 --> 00:20:37,632
I will hear the details when I visit.

343
00:20:37,716 --> 00:20:39,676
<i>Thank you very much.</i>

344
00:20:39,760 --> 00:20:42,929
I didn't expect you to accept our offer.

345
00:20:43,013 --> 00:20:45,349
I will not disappoint.

346
00:20:57,361 --> 00:21:00,322
Next, Exhibit No.7.

347
00:21:00,405 --> 00:21:03,533
This is security camera footage
from the victim's apartment.

348
00:21:03,617 --> 00:21:08,830
The defendant is seen entering and leaving
shortly before the victim's time of death,

349
00:21:08,914 --> 00:21:12,667
and with this evidence,
we plan to prove the defendant's guilt.

350
00:21:13,418 --> 00:21:16,671
After that, no one else was seen
entering or leaving the area.

351
00:21:42,823 --> 00:21:44,199
Thank you very much.

352
00:21:52,958 --> 00:21:54,543
Excuse me.

353
00:21:56,420 --> 00:21:57,462
Excuse me!

354
00:21:57,546 --> 00:21:59,714
I was saving this seat.

355
00:21:59,798 --> 00:22:01,425
What are you talking about?

356
00:22:01,508 --> 00:22:03,635
My bag… Right, my bag!

357
00:22:03,718 --> 00:22:05,053
I left my bag here.

358
00:22:05,137 --> 00:22:07,431
Do you have any proof?

359
00:22:07,514 --> 00:22:09,224
Proof?

360
00:22:09,307 --> 00:22:12,269
If you don't, stop making stuff up.

361
00:22:14,312 --> 00:22:15,730
I'm very sorry.

362
00:22:15,814 --> 00:22:17,441
There is proof.

363
00:22:28,285 --> 00:22:30,829
Huh? Mr. Uramawashi?

364
00:22:31,746 --> 00:22:33,415
How do you know of me?

365
00:22:33,498 --> 00:22:35,375
I am a lawyer too.

366
00:22:35,458 --> 00:22:36,501
So?

367
00:22:36,585 --> 00:22:39,796
I'm asking where her proof is.

368
00:22:43,258 --> 00:22:46,845
That woman over there
took a selfie earlier.

369
00:22:46,928 --> 00:22:49,306
Angle-wise, it caught this seat.

370
00:22:50,056 --> 00:22:52,475
Also, a delivery truck passed by.

371
00:22:52,559 --> 00:22:54,519
The dashcam should've caught this too.

372
00:22:54,603 --> 00:22:55,979
What?

373
00:22:56,062 --> 00:22:59,858
I've written down the plate number.
Shall we try contacting them?

374
00:23:02,485 --> 00:23:05,197
Very well. I just need to move, right?

375
00:23:06,364 --> 00:23:10,160
Only in Japan can you reserve a seat
just by leaving your bag!

376
00:23:12,871 --> 00:23:14,414
It's our victory.

377
00:23:15,081 --> 00:23:17,918
-Go ahead.
-You lied about the selfie.

378
00:23:18,001 --> 00:23:20,795
That lady doesn't seem
like she takes selfies.

379
00:23:20,879 --> 00:23:24,758
Besides,
I'm sure no delivery truck passed by.

380
00:23:26,092 --> 00:23:28,637
Your observation skills aren't half-bad.

381
00:23:28,720 --> 00:23:31,973
I don't want to sit in a seat
obtained through a lie.

382
00:23:32,057 --> 00:23:33,433
You didn't obtain it.

383
00:23:34,351 --> 00:23:37,103
You reclaimed what was yours,
through a lie.

384
00:23:43,777 --> 00:23:45,820
If there were no lies in this world,

385
00:23:45,904 --> 00:23:50,325
we would never have to doubt each other,
or worry about hidden intentions.

386
00:23:51,034 --> 00:23:52,535
Because some people lie,

387
00:23:52,619 --> 00:23:55,497
even people who do not lie
end up being suspects.

388
00:23:55,580 --> 00:23:57,707
Your ideals are beautiful.

389
00:23:57,791 --> 00:23:59,042
Is that a bad thing?

390
00:24:00,543 --> 00:24:04,130
You are like Le Corbusier's Villa Savoye.

391
00:24:08,385 --> 00:24:12,055
<i>Something urgent came up,</i>
<i>so please let me reschedule.</i>

392
00:24:12,138 --> 00:24:14,891
I don't really understand. Excuse me.

393
00:24:23,650 --> 00:24:26,194
I scanned all of her investigation files.

394
00:24:26,278 --> 00:24:27,946
How was it?

395
00:24:28,530 --> 00:24:31,741
She is not my enemy.

396
00:24:36,496 --> 00:24:39,124
Oh, you seem tired.

397
00:24:39,207 --> 00:24:41,001
A lot happened.

398
00:24:41,084 --> 00:24:43,169
Oh, hey!

399
00:24:43,253 --> 00:24:46,631
They say Yuuki Tajima is suing
this weekly magazine!

400
00:24:47,757 --> 00:24:49,634
-Due to the Chiharu article.
-Yeah.

401
00:24:49,718 --> 00:24:52,595
Attorney Uramawashi took the case.

402
00:24:52,679 --> 00:24:53,513
Huh?

403
00:24:53,596 --> 00:24:56,016
It's not related to Mr. Padam's trial,

404
00:24:56,099 --> 00:24:58,852
but you never know
what they might do, so be careful.

405
00:25:00,103 --> 00:25:04,441
Why did he agree
to defend Tajima's son anyway?

406
00:25:05,358 --> 00:25:09,029
Wouldn't it be better to defeat the son
to help that Padam guy?

407
00:25:09,863 --> 00:25:11,573
You're a real idiot, aren't you?

408
00:25:11,656 --> 00:25:12,866
An idiot?

409
00:25:12,949 --> 00:25:13,950
An idiot!

410
00:25:14,034 --> 00:25:17,704
Even if he defeats the son, he'll miss
the main target, Representative Tajima.

411
00:25:17,787 --> 00:25:20,582
He must help them in court
to gain their trust. Right?

412
00:25:20,665 --> 00:25:23,793
Very good, Nakazaki.
You aren't like Sabayama.

413
00:25:23,877 --> 00:25:26,755
-Thank you very much.
-Hey, I knew that too, you know.

414
00:25:26,838 --> 00:25:29,174
-I was just--
-Excuse me!

415
00:25:29,257 --> 00:25:31,968
-I came for an interview!
-Welcome, we've been waiting.

416
00:25:32,052 --> 00:25:33,595
-Who is that?
-Nice to meet you.

417
00:25:33,678 --> 00:25:35,096
She's interviewing for our next job.

418
00:25:35,180 --> 00:25:37,098
-Hello.
-Hello.

419
00:25:37,182 --> 00:25:38,099
TODAY'S TRENDING ARTICLE

420
00:25:38,183 --> 00:25:43,229
Because of this article, people are
leaving comments, claiming I'm the killer.

421
00:25:43,313 --> 00:25:48,902
The quickest way is to get that foreigner
named Padam to confess.

422
00:25:49,569 --> 00:25:51,279
Can you do that?

423
00:25:51,363 --> 00:25:53,281
He is ignorant of the law.

424
00:25:54,657 --> 00:25:58,495
If we tell him we'll protect his family
from forced deportation,

425
00:25:59,120 --> 00:26:00,413
he'll work with us.

426
00:26:02,248 --> 00:26:06,920
That way, Yuuki's name won't be tarnished.

427
00:26:12,801 --> 00:26:14,010
Excuse me.

428
00:26:19,265 --> 00:26:20,475
By the way,

429
00:26:21,684 --> 00:26:24,437
what were you doing
on the night of the murder?

430
00:26:26,773 --> 00:26:27,732
What?

431
00:26:29,067 --> 00:26:31,569
-Are you suspecting me?
-No.

432
00:26:32,737 --> 00:26:36,825
In order to protect you,
I want to know the truth.

433
00:26:37,951 --> 00:26:41,996
Hypothetically, even if they suspect you
are involved in the murder,

434
00:26:42,080 --> 00:26:47,293
if you tell the truth,
we can get a suspended sentence.

435
00:26:47,877 --> 00:26:49,087
Maybe.

436
00:26:51,673 --> 00:26:54,884
Depending on the intent,
the verdict varies greatly.

437
00:26:57,595 --> 00:26:59,389
I see.

438
00:27:01,141 --> 00:27:05,103
Around 7:00 p.m., the time of the crime,
where were you?

439
00:27:06,604 --> 00:27:09,274
On that day, after work,
I went out for dinner.

440
00:27:09,357 --> 00:27:10,483
Dinner?

441
00:27:11,192 --> 00:27:12,152
With whom?

442
00:27:12,777 --> 00:27:16,114
Yuuki was having dinner
with Representative Tajima.

443
00:27:16,197 --> 00:27:17,740
We have proof.

444
00:27:20,493 --> 00:27:22,912
Chiharu was just a girl
I fooled around with.

445
00:27:22,996 --> 00:27:24,831
I had no reason to kill her.

446
00:27:25,582 --> 00:27:27,417
Ever been to her apartment?

447
00:27:27,500 --> 00:27:28,751
No.

448
00:27:30,420 --> 00:27:31,296
Not even once?

449
00:27:33,798 --> 00:27:34,632
Nope.

450
00:27:35,842 --> 00:27:37,051
Very well.

451
00:27:49,564 --> 00:27:51,941
LEMON GASUI

452
00:29:15,984 --> 00:29:17,527
It's done.

453
00:29:20,864 --> 00:29:23,032
A blueprint of lies.

454
00:29:24,742 --> 00:29:27,161
Ms. Konno, room B, please.

455
00:29:27,245 --> 00:29:28,788
The most expensive spot.

456
00:29:28,872 --> 00:29:32,667
-Habu, take the dimensions from the model.
-Got it. I'll draft the layouts.

457
00:29:32,750 --> 00:29:34,919
Is this 1 to 30?
Match it with the wall surface.

458
00:29:35,003 --> 00:29:37,589
-I know.
-Nakazaki, samples for the cross-panels.

459
00:29:37,672 --> 00:29:38,548
Okay.

460
00:29:38,631 --> 00:29:42,093
Sabayama, verify the materials
and list interior finishes and equipment.

461
00:29:42,176 --> 00:29:45,054
-Okay.
-Oh, right. Ms. Konno.

462
00:29:45,889 --> 00:29:47,515
Handle this too.

463
00:29:48,433 --> 00:29:49,809
What is this for?

464
00:29:49,893 --> 00:29:52,729
-Won't concrete work for the aging finish?
-I know.

465
00:29:52,812 --> 00:29:56,065
-Search online for the circled parts here.
-Excuse me.

466
00:29:56,149 --> 00:29:59,736
I am Yukari Aso,
an attorney from Cordia Law Firm.

467
00:30:03,656 --> 00:30:04,657
Huh?

468
00:30:04,741 --> 00:30:07,452
Wait, is this Mr. Uramawashi's office?

469
00:30:07,535 --> 00:30:09,537
Mr. Uramawashi is in that room.

470
00:30:10,413 --> 00:30:13,124
I'm sorry. Excuse me.

471
00:30:13,207 --> 00:30:14,542
Sorry.

472
00:30:18,880 --> 00:30:20,590
Have we met somewhere before?

473
00:30:20,673 --> 00:30:22,800
-No. This is our first meeting.
-No…

474
00:30:22,884 --> 00:30:25,428
-I've met you--
-Why have you come to see him?

475
00:30:25,511 --> 00:30:27,555
-I will guide you.
-No need.

476
00:30:31,392 --> 00:30:33,019
Mr. Uramawashi. Excuse me!

477
00:30:33,102 --> 00:30:36,356
I am Yukari Aso,
an attorney from Cordia Law Firm.

478
00:30:37,065 --> 00:30:38,524
I met you the other day.

479
00:30:38,608 --> 00:30:40,610
Mr. Padam suddenly confessed.

480
00:30:40,693 --> 00:30:42,528
What on earth did you say to him?

481
00:30:43,112 --> 00:30:46,866
The person who killed Chiharu Aoi
might be Yuuki Tajima.

482
00:30:46,950 --> 00:30:49,994
They used influence
to pin the crime on Mr. Padam.

483
00:30:51,621 --> 00:30:53,957
Hey, what are you doing?

484
00:30:54,040 --> 00:30:55,750
I'm in the middle of an interview.

485
00:31:05,510 --> 00:31:07,595
This lawyer is calling me a killer.

486
00:31:07,679 --> 00:31:09,722
I'm going to sue her for defamation!

487
00:31:09,806 --> 00:31:10,640
What?

488
00:31:10,723 --> 00:31:13,017
Why her and not the publisher?

489
00:31:13,101 --> 00:31:15,103
It will show them we mean business.

490
00:31:15,186 --> 00:31:16,354
Wait a minute.

491
00:31:16,437 --> 00:31:20,358
What if this creates more trouble?
Making an enemy out of a lawyer--

492
00:31:20,441 --> 00:31:21,818
Don't interfere!

493
00:31:26,155 --> 00:31:27,657
Mr. Uramawashi.

494
00:31:28,449 --> 00:31:30,827
I leave this up to you.

495
00:31:33,538 --> 00:31:35,248
TOKYO DISTRICT COURT

496
00:31:39,585 --> 00:31:43,464
INDICTMENT
DEFENDANT - YUKARI ASO

497
00:31:46,092 --> 00:31:48,886
Ms. Aso, don't worry.
Even if you lose the trial, it's okay.

498
00:31:48,970 --> 00:31:51,848
It's not like your life is over.
Just do your best.

499
00:31:53,224 --> 00:31:57,562
No, I can't help.
I'm insanely busy right now.

500
00:31:57,645 --> 00:31:59,147
It's fine.

501
00:31:59,230 --> 00:32:01,024
I will defend myself.

502
00:32:01,566 --> 00:32:05,820
What wins in court is not influence,
but justice, right?

503
00:32:07,363 --> 00:32:09,032
Thanks for waiting!

504
00:32:09,115 --> 00:32:10,283
I'm here.

505
00:32:10,366 --> 00:32:12,493
Sorry, my mistake!

506
00:32:12,577 --> 00:32:13,953
There you are!

507
00:32:16,289 --> 00:32:20,251
I got plenty of cute girls
for you, Mr. Uramawashi.

508
00:32:20,334 --> 00:32:21,627
Why thank you.

509
00:32:21,711 --> 00:32:24,338
I'll stick with you all night.

510
00:32:25,298 --> 00:32:29,969
Alright, then,
as a rally before the decisive battle,

511
00:32:30,053 --> 00:32:32,221
everyone's drinking tonight!

512
00:32:32,305 --> 00:32:34,766
Yay! Cheers!

513
00:32:34,849 --> 00:32:36,267
-First time here?
-Yes.

514
00:32:36,350 --> 00:32:37,810
I'm Ai. Nice to meet you.

515
00:32:37,894 --> 00:32:40,313
-Nice, Ai! Let's toast!
-Hang on!

516
00:32:40,396 --> 00:32:41,814
-Here, Ai.
-May I?

517
00:32:41,898 --> 00:32:44,317
-Cheers.
-Cheers.

518
00:32:51,866 --> 00:32:53,326
Hey, Yuuki.

519
00:32:53,409 --> 00:32:54,660
Let's go home together.

520
00:32:54,744 --> 00:32:56,079
Should we?

521
00:32:56,162 --> 00:32:57,663
Sorry, I'll head out first!

522
00:32:58,748 --> 00:33:00,875
Mr. Uramawashi, I'm heading out.

523
00:33:00,958 --> 00:33:03,586
-Allow me to drive you two home.
-Really?

524
00:33:03,669 --> 00:33:04,754
I haven't drunk.

525
00:33:04,837 --> 00:33:06,798
-How nice!
-You mean it?

526
00:33:06,881 --> 00:33:08,966
-Well then, please do.
-Huh?

527
00:33:27,777 --> 00:33:29,237
Ai?

528
00:33:43,251 --> 00:33:44,460
Huh?

529
00:33:49,757 --> 00:33:51,008
What?

530
00:33:52,426 --> 00:33:53,636
This room…

531
00:33:55,096 --> 00:33:55,930
What?

532
00:33:58,641 --> 00:34:00,476
Will you be all right tomorrow?

533
00:34:01,310 --> 00:34:04,188
At the last hearing,
I pointed out traces of editing

534
00:34:04,272 --> 00:34:06,858
in the apartment's CCTV footage,

535
00:34:07,775 --> 00:34:10,862
and they haven't been able to explain it.

536
00:34:11,696 --> 00:34:15,324
I believe they edited the footage
to remove Yuuki Tajima from it.

537
00:34:15,408 --> 00:34:17,785
Then, you will go all out.

538
00:34:18,411 --> 00:34:19,412
Yes!

539
00:34:22,039 --> 00:34:25,334
<i>We will now begin the witness examination.</i>

540
00:34:25,918 --> 00:34:30,381
Regarding the CCTV footage
claim made by the defendant last time,

541
00:34:30,464 --> 00:34:33,926
we have Mr. Igawa,
the apartment manager, joining us.

542
00:34:34,635 --> 00:34:39,182
You were habitually committing mail theft.

543
00:34:40,099 --> 00:34:45,771
In order to erase that evidence,
you edited the security camera footage.

544
00:34:45,855 --> 00:34:47,231
What?

545
00:34:47,982 --> 00:34:49,734
I am very sorry.

546
00:34:49,817 --> 00:34:54,780
There is no footage remaining
from the day of the incident.

547
00:34:56,282 --> 00:34:57,116
Correct.

548
00:34:57,200 --> 00:34:58,201
Objection!

549
00:34:58,951 --> 00:35:00,870
Are you covering for someone?

550
00:35:00,953 --> 00:35:02,371
Please speak truthfully.

551
00:35:02,455 --> 00:35:03,623
I'm not lying!

552
00:35:04,248 --> 00:35:05,541
It's the truth.

553
00:35:20,264 --> 00:35:21,807
PLAINTIFF EXAMINATION

554
00:35:23,851 --> 00:35:27,688
We will now begin
the examination of the plaintiff himself.

555
00:35:27,772 --> 00:35:30,233
Plaintiff's counsel, please proceed.

556
00:35:33,778 --> 00:35:34,987
Mr. Tajima,

557
00:35:36,405 --> 00:35:43,371
the defendant stated to a reporter
that you murdered Chiharu Aoi.

558
00:35:43,454 --> 00:35:45,414
Is this true or false?

559
00:35:45,998 --> 00:35:47,333
False.

560
00:35:47,416 --> 00:35:49,669
You have never been to her place either.

561
00:35:49,752 --> 00:35:51,045
Of course not.

562
00:35:51,921 --> 00:35:57,593
Your Honor,
may I ask questions using Exhibit No.5?

563
00:35:57,677 --> 00:35:58,928
Granted.

564
00:36:02,348 --> 00:36:03,557
Huh? This…

565
00:36:03,641 --> 00:36:07,728
This room is an exact recreation
of the room where Ms. Aoi lived,

566
00:36:07,812 --> 00:36:10,022
before she was murdered.

567
00:36:10,106 --> 00:36:12,525
What is the meaning of this?

568
00:36:12,608 --> 00:36:15,319
I took the liberty of testing you
based on my judgment.

569
00:36:15,403 --> 00:36:16,320
Testing?

570
00:36:16,404 --> 00:36:18,614
It is to protect you.

571
00:36:19,824 --> 00:36:24,495
Hypothetically, if Mr. Tajima
had murdered Ms. Aoi,

572
00:36:25,413 --> 00:36:29,959
waking up and realizing he is at her place
should make him agitated, but!

573
00:36:30,042 --> 00:36:31,210
Take a look.

574
00:36:31,877 --> 00:36:34,630
He is completely calm.

575
00:36:34,714 --> 00:36:36,549
He is clearly agitated.

576
00:36:38,551 --> 00:36:39,760
<i>Huh?</i>

577
00:36:41,304 --> 00:36:44,682
Then, inconveniently, a blackout happened.

578
00:36:45,599 --> 00:36:47,935
He is obviously agitated, isn't he?

579
00:36:48,019 --> 00:36:52,023
-Why does he know where the breaker is?
-Please don't speak out of line.

580
00:36:52,106 --> 00:36:56,277
You just happened
to see the breaker, right?

581
00:36:56,360 --> 00:36:57,653
That's right.

582
00:37:04,535 --> 00:37:08,414
Even when running out of the room,
the plaintiff avoided a specific spot!

583
00:37:08,497 --> 00:37:11,542
That is the spot where
Ms. Aoi was found dead.

584
00:37:11,625 --> 00:37:13,377
You have been there before!

585
00:37:13,461 --> 00:37:15,755
Please do not speak out of line.

586
00:37:15,838 --> 00:37:20,843
Ms. Aso's statements are all forced logic.

587
00:37:20,926 --> 00:37:24,638
But… You can't dismiss this
as mere coincidence.

588
00:37:25,681 --> 00:37:27,892
If you want to make that claim,

589
00:37:28,684 --> 00:37:33,314
there is one more
piece of evidence that solidifies

590
00:37:34,523 --> 00:37:35,775
Mr. Tajima's innocence.

591
00:37:38,069 --> 00:37:40,363
Mr. Igawa, the apartment manager,

592
00:37:40,446 --> 00:37:43,532
deleted the CCTV footage
from the day of the murder,

593
00:37:43,616 --> 00:37:45,743
to hide his own theft.

594
00:37:47,370 --> 00:37:48,454
But we recovered it.

595
00:37:50,414 --> 00:37:51,457
Order in the court!

596
00:37:53,292 --> 00:37:55,086
If you check this,

597
00:37:55,169 --> 00:37:58,964
you will see that Mr. Tajima
does not appear on camera.

598
00:37:59,048 --> 00:38:00,132
Hey!

599
00:38:02,551 --> 00:38:05,346
With this, your innocence will be proven.

600
00:38:05,429 --> 00:38:06,889
Wait! Stop going off-script!

601
00:38:06,972 --> 00:38:08,224
Order in the court!

602
00:38:16,190 --> 00:38:19,819
I found it in your car the other day,
when I was driving you home.

603
00:38:21,612 --> 00:38:22,613
No…

604
00:38:22,696 --> 00:38:23,781
It's not mine!

605
00:38:24,865 --> 00:38:28,744
Isn't that the nail that was on
Ms. Aoi's index finger?

606
00:38:29,954 --> 00:38:32,623
The corpse's index finger
was missing its nail.

607
00:38:32,706 --> 00:38:34,917
It came off while you were fighting?

608
00:38:35,000 --> 00:38:36,001
Impossible!

609
00:38:36,585 --> 00:38:37,795
There's just no way!

610
00:38:37,878 --> 00:38:40,881
So the one who killed
Aoi Chiharu really was you!

611
00:38:40,965 --> 00:38:43,008
That is merely your speculation.

612
00:38:45,553 --> 00:38:48,013
Yuuki, calm down.

613
00:38:48,639 --> 00:38:51,809
If I show this footage,
the truth will be revealed.

614
00:38:53,561 --> 00:38:57,231
Your Honor, please play the video.

615
00:38:58,858 --> 00:39:01,360
-She fell on her own!
-Yuuki!

616
00:39:01,444 --> 00:39:03,904
-I didn't kill her!
-Yuuki!

617
00:39:11,287 --> 00:39:13,289
Please wait a moment.

618
00:39:14,331 --> 00:39:15,833
Does that mean

619
00:39:17,376 --> 00:39:19,837
you were lying?

620
00:39:20,546 --> 00:39:21,589
Am I correct?

621
00:39:21,672 --> 00:39:23,507
It was an accident!

622
00:39:23,591 --> 00:39:26,969
I just pushed her, and she fell,
I had no intent to kill her!

623
00:39:27,052 --> 00:39:29,972
If I tell the truth,
I'll get a suspended sentence, right?

624
00:39:35,728 --> 00:39:37,229
Your lies…

625
00:39:37,980 --> 00:39:39,356
have no beauty to them.

626
00:39:44,778 --> 00:39:46,405
Attorney Aso.

627
00:39:48,407 --> 00:39:50,659
Things have taken an unexpected turn.

628
00:39:50,743 --> 00:39:54,497
While I do regret it, I wish you the best.

629
00:39:55,664 --> 00:39:56,499
Your Honor.

630
00:39:57,458 --> 00:40:00,252
I have no further questions.

631
00:40:19,021 --> 00:40:21,148
Ai, you did great.

632
00:40:21,232 --> 00:40:22,274
Two envelopes?

633
00:40:22,358 --> 00:40:24,610
We'll call you when we need you again.

634
00:40:24,693 --> 00:40:26,529
Wait, you're paying me this much?

635
00:40:26,612 --> 00:40:30,491
In the end, he was lying about restoring
the CCTV footage, right?

636
00:40:30,574 --> 00:40:31,534
-Yeah.
-Yeah!

637
00:40:31,617 --> 00:40:33,244
That disc was empty.

638
00:40:33,827 --> 00:40:37,081
The nail was also fake. We copied it
from Chiharu's social media.

639
00:40:37,164 --> 00:40:41,377
By pretending to save the son,
he got close to Representative Tajima.

640
00:40:41,961 --> 00:40:44,838
In doing so,
he ended up taking down both of them.

641
00:40:44,922 --> 00:40:47,049
-A job well done.
-Nakazaki.

642
00:40:47,132 --> 00:40:49,760
-Yes!
-Can I take all this with me?

643
00:40:49,843 --> 00:40:51,845
-Sure.
-Here we go.

644
00:40:51,929 --> 00:40:56,809
By the way, that alibi photo,
he knew it was fake from the start.

645
00:40:56,892 --> 00:40:59,186
-Really?
-Hey, out of the way!

646
00:40:59,270 --> 00:41:00,688
The road in the background…

647
00:41:00,771 --> 00:41:03,023
At 7:00 p.m. that day,
there was no traffic jam.

648
00:41:03,107 --> 00:41:06,402
So he knew and played along!

649
00:41:06,485 --> 00:41:08,320
I'm glad he's our ally.

650
00:41:08,404 --> 00:41:10,281
As an enemy, he's terrifying!

651
00:41:16,078 --> 00:41:19,790
<i>Naoto Uramawashi, you committed acts</i>
<i>against the interests of your client,</i>

652
00:41:19,873 --> 00:41:23,877
and violated your duty of good faith.

653
00:41:25,129 --> 00:41:28,340
Pursuant to Article 56,
Paragraph One of the Attorneys Act,

654
00:41:28,424 --> 00:41:31,218
you are hereby suspended from practice.

655
00:41:31,302 --> 00:41:34,430
You are not fit to be a lawyer.

656
00:41:35,306 --> 00:41:36,890
Do you have any last words?

657
00:41:46,066 --> 00:41:48,360
Eileen Gray once said…

658
00:41:48,444 --> 00:41:50,696
"To create,

659
00:41:51,488 --> 00:41:54,283
one must first question everything."

660
00:41:55,701 --> 00:41:56,910
That's all.

661
00:42:02,333 --> 00:42:03,792
Eileen?

662
00:42:04,585 --> 00:42:05,794
Who's that?

663
00:42:06,295 --> 00:42:07,671
Do you know?

664
00:42:09,965 --> 00:42:12,801
The Japanese branch is now on track.

665
00:42:12,885 --> 00:42:15,012
Yes, impressive.

666
00:42:17,097 --> 00:42:18,390
Like father, like son.

667
00:42:18,474 --> 00:42:20,059
Thank you very much.

668
00:42:21,727 --> 00:42:23,604
You have a guest.

669
00:42:25,731 --> 00:42:27,107
Sorry to disturb your meal.

670
00:42:27,733 --> 00:42:28,942
Mr. Furuse!

671
00:42:29,026 --> 00:42:30,110
I am…

672
00:42:30,194 --> 00:42:32,446
I am sorry for being late.

673
00:42:32,529 --> 00:42:33,822
Sorry for--

674
00:42:33,906 --> 00:42:37,451
My office received some photos,
sent anonymously.

675
00:42:37,534 --> 00:42:40,079
-Oh.
-Along with proof of your illegal conduct.

676
00:42:40,162 --> 00:42:40,996
What?

677
00:42:45,542 --> 00:42:48,587
Was it Mr. Ishikawa?
So you were meeting with him?

678
00:42:49,672 --> 00:42:52,049
-This…
-Are you hiding something from me?

679
00:42:54,009 --> 00:42:55,052
I am very sorry!

680
00:42:55,761 --> 00:42:58,972
-But--
-Please, stand up.

681
00:43:00,766 --> 00:43:02,976
Your son's problem is more important.

682
00:43:03,727 --> 00:43:06,021
It is no longer just your personal issue,

683
00:43:06,105 --> 00:43:08,774
it could spell trouble
for our entire party.

684
00:43:08,857 --> 00:43:10,317
You understand, right?

685
00:43:12,027 --> 00:43:13,654
My apologies, but…

686
00:43:15,572 --> 00:43:16,949
Murata.

687
00:43:17,032 --> 00:43:19,618
I'll need you to come back here soon.

688
00:43:19,702 --> 00:43:20,828
I understand.

689
00:43:20,911 --> 00:43:22,913
-Sorry.
-Wait!

690
00:43:22,996 --> 00:43:25,457
-It's no problem.
-Mr. Tajima.

691
00:43:25,541 --> 00:43:29,211
Sir! Wait…

692
00:43:29,294 --> 00:43:30,796
This is good!

693
00:43:30,879 --> 00:43:32,214
Right?

694
00:43:32,297 --> 00:43:35,175
I'm glad Mr. Padam got an acquittal.

695
00:43:35,259 --> 00:43:36,719
Thank you very much.

696
00:43:36,802 --> 00:43:40,180
I don't want to admit it,
but it's thanks to Mr. Uramawashi.

697
00:43:40,264 --> 00:43:41,223
Is that so?

698
00:43:41,807 --> 00:43:45,853
Good timing, then.
I'd like to ask you to monitor him.

699
00:43:45,936 --> 00:43:46,979
Huh?

700
00:43:47,688 --> 00:43:50,774
If he keeps on being reckless,

701
00:43:50,858 --> 00:43:54,111
it will affect the credibility
of our bar association.

702
00:43:54,194 --> 00:43:58,657
-I'm asking you, as the President--
-Wait, I can't do it!

703
00:43:58,741 --> 00:44:00,284
I really can't.

704
00:44:00,367 --> 00:44:05,205
Because you were sued, our office
was busy handling complaints, you know.

705
00:44:06,623 --> 00:44:08,959
It was really tough!

706
00:44:10,002 --> 00:44:11,462
I'll do it.

707
00:44:13,046 --> 00:44:13,881
Thank you.

708
00:44:15,090 --> 00:44:18,844
I'm not asking you to see him daily.
Just check on him a few days a week.

709
00:44:19,762 --> 00:44:20,846
Okay.

710
00:44:21,972 --> 00:44:24,933
Besides, he said you passed, too.

711
00:44:25,017 --> 00:44:27,394
-What are you talking about?
-Do your best.

712
00:44:29,229 --> 00:44:32,274
So, I will be visiting you starting today.

713
00:44:36,278 --> 00:44:39,114
Don't fool around.
We have to start closing your office.

714
00:44:39,198 --> 00:44:42,075
Delete your home page,
hide any signs you have outside.

715
00:44:42,159 --> 00:44:43,869
I don't have either.

716
00:44:43,952 --> 00:44:45,871
Please don't lie to me.

717
00:44:46,538 --> 00:44:51,001
I was so busy suing you, Aso,
my architectural work has been piling up.

718
00:44:51,084 --> 00:44:51,960
What?

719
00:44:52,044 --> 00:44:54,171
Mr. Uramawashi, you are an architect?

720
00:45:04,014 --> 00:45:07,518
More importantly,
when did you start lying?

721
00:45:08,685 --> 00:45:10,687
Did you leak info to the weekly magazine

722
00:45:10,771 --> 00:45:13,232
so that Yuuki Tajima
would request your defense?

723
00:45:13,315 --> 00:45:17,236
Did you sue me in a civil trial
just to drag him to court?

724
00:45:17,861 --> 00:45:19,571
Not bad.

725
00:45:20,531 --> 00:45:22,157
But it's all so boring.

726
00:45:25,494 --> 00:45:27,412
Please, at least answer me this.

727
00:45:27,496 --> 00:45:29,790
Why did you get suspended
from being a lawyer?

728
00:45:30,582 --> 00:45:32,501
For someone as sharp as you,

729
00:45:32,584 --> 00:45:36,797
there must have been ways to corner
the Tajimas without being suspended!

730
00:45:39,633 --> 00:45:41,552
I got tired of being a lawyer.

731
00:45:41,635 --> 00:45:42,886
-What?
-That's a lie.

732
00:45:43,595 --> 00:45:44,805
What?!

733
00:45:46,056 --> 00:45:48,892
Right now, you are an architect,
not a lawyer!

734
00:45:49,560 --> 00:45:52,646
<i>The evidence of his violence</i>
<i>still remains in the video!</i>

735
00:45:52,729 --> 00:45:55,983
<i>-He hasn't found out yet?</i>
<i>-I will fight fair and square and win.</i>

736
00:45:56,066 --> 00:45:59,486
<i>If they become the main developers,</i>
<i>they can make a lot more money…</i>

737
00:45:59,570 --> 00:46:00,612
<i>His lies.</i>

738
00:46:00,696 --> 00:46:01,738
I'll expose them.

739
00:46:01,822 --> 00:46:06,535
Careless words invite ruin.
I'll make sure you never defend again.

740
00:46:07,202 --> 00:46:08,161
Subtitle translation by: Nix S.

